export anchor RunningExample:
    description:
        The chapters of this section follow one small specification from
        start to finish. It is written the way specifications usually are: a
        little structure, and prose doing most of the work.

    source:
        The file is button.pi.

        ```piton
        export anchor Button:
            description:
                A button is something that can be clicked. When clicked, its
                action is invoked.

                The button is blue. It can be enabled or disabled.

            disabled:
                Its color is dimmed. Its text is dimmed. It cannot be clicked.
        ```

    whatAPersonReadsInIt:
        A careful reader comes away knowing this.

        ```text
        A button can be clicked, and clicking it invokes its action.
        It is blue.
        It is either enabled or disabled.
        While disabled, its color and its text are dimmed, and it cannot be clicked.
        ```

        The same careful reader also knows what it does not say: what the
        action is, what the text is, and what dimming means.

    whatAnalysisDerives:
        By the end of this section, analysis will have turned it into this.
        Every line can be traced back to the words above, and nothing in it
        was guessed.

        ```text
        Button.state is one of enabled, disabled        stated
        Button.color = blue                              stated
        when Button.state = enabled:
            Button can be clicked                        derived
            on Button clicked: invoke Button.action      derived
        when Button.state = disabled:
            Button.color = dim(Button.color)             stated
            Button.text = dim(Button.text)               stated
            Button cannot be clicked                     stated
            on Button clicked: Button.action is not invoked   derived

        open: Button.action is used but never defined
        open: dim is applied but never defined
        open: Button.text is used but never defined
        ```

        Two things are worth noticing already. Several of the most useful
        lines, such as the button being clickable only while enabled, were
        never written by the author; they follow from what was. And the three
        open lines are not failures. They are exactly what the careful reader
        noticed was missing, found mechanically.
